{"ts":"2026-10-09T09:18:32.203Z","tool":"execute_code","type":"tool","status":"ERROR","ms":2713,"action":"execute","params":{"action":"execute","code":"// Add visual representation to EnemyTank\nGameObject enemyTank = GameObject.Find(\"EnemyTank\");\nif (enemyTank == null) { return \"Enemy not found\"; }\n\n// Add visual body\nMeshFilter mf = enemyTank.GetComponent<MeshFilter>();\nif (mf == null) mf = enemyTank.AddComponent<MeshFilter>();\nif (mf.sharedMesh == null)\n{\n    mf.sharedMesh = GameObject.CreatePrimitive(PrimitiveType.Capsule).GetComponent<MeshFilter>().sharedMesh;\n    // Clean up temp object\n    var temp = GameObject.CreatePrimitive(PrimitiveType.Capsule);\n    Object.DestroyImmediate(temp);\n}\n\nMeshRenderer mr = enemyTank.GetComponent<MeshRenderer>();\nif (mr == null) mr = enemyTank.AddComponent<MeshRenderer>();\nif (mr.sharedMaterial == null)\n{\n    // Create a simple red material\n    Shader shader = Shader.Find(\"Universal Render Pipeline/Lit\");\n    if (shader == null) shader = Shader.Find(\"Standard\");\n    Material mat = new Material(shader);\n    mat.color = new Color(0.8f, 0.2f, 0.2f);\n    mr.sharedMaterial = mat;\n}\n\n// Make EnemyTank navigation static for NavMesh (it moves with NavMeshAgent, so don't set static)\n// But the Turret child should be static relative to the tank\n\nreturn \"EnemyTank visual setup complete\";","safety_checks":true,"compiler":"auto"},"error":"Compilation failed"}
